<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gustav Mahler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1860">1860</a>–<a href="/years/1911">1911</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mahler</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gustav Mahler was an Austrian composer and conductor, known for his large-scale symphonies and song cycles. He served as director of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> Court Opera. He is counted among the figures of the cultural flowering of Vienna under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gustav-mahler.jpg" alt="Gustav Mahler" width="320" height="382" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moritz Nähr · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Photo_of_Gustav_Mahler_by_Moritz_N%C3%A4hr_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
